# JAN: Jump if A Negative - 8-bit mask instruction
# YAML: mask "1111_1111_0000_0000", opcode "0130400" (octal)
# Conditional jump based on A register sign bit
#
# C# EMULATOR ANALYSIS COMPLETE
# Source: E:\Dev\Repos\Ronny\RetroCore\Emulated.HW\ND\CPU\ND100\Instructions.SequencingInstructions.cs:93
#
# VERIFIED BEHAVIOR FROM C# EMULATOR:
# 1. Condition evaluation:
#    - condition = ((regs.currentRegisters.A & (1 << 15)) != 0)
#    - Tests bit 15 of A register (sign bit for 2's complement)
#
# 2. Jump conditions:
#    - JUMP: A[15] == 1 (A register negative in 2's complement)
#    - NO JUMP: A[15] == 0 (A register positive or zero)
#
# 3. Address calculation:
#    - Target = (PC - 1) + displacement
#    - Range: -128 to +127 words (signed 8-bit displacement)
#
:JAN disp is op8=0xB1 & disp {  # 0130400 octal = 0xB100, mask 1111_1111_0000_0000 (8 bits), pattern 0xB1
    # FIXED IMPLEMENTATION: Use same pattern as working JMP instruction
    local addr:2 = inst_start + 1 + disp;  # Calculate PC-relative target (same as JMP)
    if ((A & 0x8000) != 0) goto [addr];  # Jump if A negative (sign bit set)
}
# SLEIGH Pattern Works: x86 and 68000 use identical "if (condition) goto constructor" pattern